Convert to minutes:

$$
\frac{9}{2.75} = \frac{9}{2.75} = \frac{900}{275} = \frac{36}{11} \text{ hours}
$$

$$
\frac{36}{11} \times 60 = \frac{2160}{11} \approx 196.36 \text{ minutes}
$$

But the question is: **the number of minutes the walk takes her, including the t minutes spent in the coffee shop**.

So we need to add t = 139.7 minutes to the time taken to walk at 2.75 km/h.

So:

$$
\text{Total time} = \frac{2160}{11} + 139.7 \approx 196.36 + 139.7 = 336.06 \text{ minutes}
$$

So the final answer is:

$$
\boxed{336}
