\binom{4}{2} \cdot \binom{6}{2} + \binom{4}{3} \cdot \binom{6}{1} + \binom{4}{4} \cdot \binom{6}{0}
$$

$$
= 6 \cdot 15 + 4 \cdot 6 + 1 \cdot 1 = 90 + 24 + 1 = 115
$$

So the total number of such pairs is:

$$
\binom{10}{4} \cdot 115 = 210 \cdot 115 = 24150
$$

So:

$$
\mathbb{P}(B) = \frac{24150}{\binom{10}{4}^2} = \frac{24150}{210^2} = \frac{24150}{44100} = \frac{161}{294}
$$

